.Dd 2026-06-02
.Dt NOMAD-RESET-OLLAMA 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nomad-reset-ollama
.Nd recover the native Ollama daemon from a stuck state
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm nomad reset-ollama
.Op Fl -internal | Fl -drive
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reloads the native Ollama LaunchAgent: it boots the agent out, kills any
orphan
.Ic ollama serve
processes, confirms port 11434 is free, re-bootstraps the agent, and waits
for the API to come back up.
Reach for it when Ollama is wedged, after an upgrade, or when the model store
has changed.
.Pp
On the oMLX backend,
.Nm
resets the whole oMLX stack instead \(em the oMLX server
.Pq Li :8000 ,
the Ollama-compat proxy
.Pq Li :11436 ,
the embed-only Ollama
.Pq Li :11435 ,
and the coexisting general Ollama
.Pq Li :11434 \(em
re-bootstrapping each and waiting for the proxy to answer.
.Pp
Before touching launchd,
.Nm
decides which model store to serve from so the daemon resolves the right one
on its first spawn.
With no flag it auto-detects.
If an external data drive is configured but its model store is wedged
.Pq a deep read does not return ,
.Nm
falls back to the internal store
.Pq Pa ~/.ollama/models
and warns that a physical unplug and replug is required; a later run
auto-restores the drive once it reads healthy again.
.Pp
When running on the internal store and that store is empty,
.Nm
auto-pulls a model set sized to this Mac's RAM.
The pull is disk-gated, downshifting to a smaller tier so it fits the boot
volume, and is best-effort: a failed or partial pull does not fail the reset,
since the daemon is already up.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -internal
Force the internal model store regardless of drive state.
.It Fl -drive
Restore to the external data drive's model store.
Refused if no data drive or model store is found, or if the drive is still
wedged; in the wedged case, unplug and replug the drive physically, then
retry.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic nomad reset-ollama
Reload the daemon, auto-detecting the model store and falling back to internal
if the drive is wedged.
.It Ic nomad reset-ollama --internal
Reload and force the internal model store.
.It Ic nomad reset-ollama --drive
Reload and restore the drive-backed store, once the drive is healthy.
.El
.Sh TROUBLESHOOTING
.Ss Missing llama.cpp runner
If the Ollama daemon answers
.Pq Li /api/tags
but every model load fails with HTTP 500
.Dq llama-server binary not found ,
the llama.cpp inference runner is absent from the install.
A known cause on macOS 26
.Pq Tahoe
is the Homebrew ollama
.Em formula
bottle, which ships runner-less
.Pq only the MLX runner ,
breaking both chat on port 11434 and RAG embeddings on port 11435 while the
API still looks healthy.
.Pp
.Ic nomad check
flags this with a real inference probe rather than only a port check.
Reinstalling the formula does not help \(em
.Ic brew reinstall
re-pours the same runner-less bottle.
Restore the runner with the official app, then run
.Ic nomad reset-ollama :
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Ic brew install --cask ollama
.Pq the official app bundles a complete runner
.It
or download from
.Lk https://ollama.com/download/mac
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nomad 1 ,
.Xr nomad-check 1 ,
.Xr nomad-models 1 ,
.Xr nomad-upgrade-models 1
